# CLAIM

**1.** A method for coordinating delayed video streaming and subtitle timing signals in a communication network, the network comprising a controller, a communication unit, a subtitler terminal, and a viewer terminal, the method comprising:

receiving, at the communication unit, a video stream from a media source, the video stream comprising a plurality of video frames each associated with a respective timestamp;

buffering, by the communication unit, the video stream for a predetermined delay period prior to transmission to the viewer terminal, so as to establish a delay interval between a live presentation time of the video stream and a delivery time of the video stream to the viewer terminal;

transmitting, by the communication unit, a first instance of the video stream to the subtitler terminal substantially in real time, independent of the predetermined delay period;

receiving, at the subtitler terminal, the first instance of the video stream and generating, in response to viewing the first instance of the video stream, subtitle data corresponding to spoken content within the video frames, the subtitle data comprising a plurality of subtitle segments each associated with a generation timestamp indicative of a time at which the respective subtitle segment was generated relative to the video stream;

transmitting the subtitle data from the subtitler terminal to the controller;

determining, by the controller, a timing offset based on a comparison between the generation timestamp of each subtitle segment and the predetermined delay period applied to the video stream by the communication unit;

generating, by the controller, a subtitle timing signal for each subtitle segment based on the determined timing offset, the subtitle timing signal indicating a synchronized presentation time at which the respective subtitle segment is to be presented relative to the delayed video stream at the viewer terminal;

transmitting, by the communication unit, a second instance of the video stream, delayed by the predetermined delay period, to the viewer terminal together with the subtitle timing signal and corresponding subtitle segment; and

presenting, at the viewer terminal, the subtitle segment in synchronization with the second instance of the video stream according to the synchronized presentation time indicated by the subtitle timing signal, such that the subtitle segment is displayed concurrently with the spoken content corresponding thereto within the delayed video stream.
